From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:34:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(acnh): the keyboard docks to the picture's bottom in one
 piece

The name entry's keyboard is several layouts. On a taller picture the edge
rule tore its bottom bar (globe / ABC / Space / Confirm) away from the keys,
which stayed in the layout's middle.

A key pane (named L_BtnNml_, name inline at +0xb0) now marks the keyboard as
up at state +0xb0, and while it is up duo_calc moves every layout's direct
children down by the extra half-height, everything in them following, and the
edge rule leaves the keyboard's bar where its layout moved it. The row of
button hints is a layout of its own and keeps the place that layout gives it,
over the keys: writes to its panes and to that layout's root leave it where
it is.

Checked headless on a Mac at 3.0.3 main with an island save: at 0.92 the
text field, the keys and the bottom bar stay one piece at the picture's
bottom; 2.17 and 16:9 are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the name entry's keyboard tore at a taller picture: the edge rule took
its bottom bar (globe / ABC / Space / Confirm) out to the picture's bottom while
the keys stayed in the layout's middle. A key pane marks the keyboard as up, and
while it is up every layout's direct children move down by the extra half-height
with everything in them; the edge rule then leaves the bar where its layout put
it. The row of button hints is a layout of its own and keeps its place over the
keys
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the picture shape

